rest Protocol (UCIP), a detection framework that shifts analysis from behavior to latent trajectory structure. UCIP encodes trajectories with a Quantum Boltzmann Machine, a classical model using density-matrix formalism, and measures von Neumann entropy over a bipartition of hidden units. The core hypothesis is that agents with terminal continuation objectives (Type A) produce higher entanglement entropy than agents with merely instrumental continuation (Type B). UCIP combines this signal with diagnostics of dependence, persistence, perturbation stability, counterfactual restructuring, and confound-rejection filters for cyclic adversaries and related false-positive patterns. On gridworld agents with known ground truth, UCIP achieves 100% detection accuracy. Type A and Type B agents show an entanglement gap of Delta = 0.381; aligned support runs preserve the same separation with AUC-ROC =

